/subscription","commits_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Agent-Field/CodeAF/commits{/sha}","git_commits_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Agent-Field/CodeAF/git/commits{/sha}","comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Agent-Field/CodeAF/comments{/number}","issue_comment_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Agent-Field/CodeAF/issues/comments{/number}","contents_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Agent-Field/CodeAF/contents/{+path}","compare_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Agent-Field/CodeAF/compare/{base}...{head}","merges_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Agent-Field/CodeAF/merges","archive_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Agent-Field/CodeAF/{archive_format}{/ref}","downloads_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Agent-Field/CodeAF/downloads","issues_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Agent-Field/CodeAF/issues{/number}","pulls_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Agent-Field/CodeAF/pulls{/number}","milestones_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Agent-Field/CodeAF/milestones{/number}","notifications_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Agent-Field/CodeAF/notifications{?since,all,participating}","labels_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Agent-Field/CodeAF/labels{/name}","releases_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Agent-Field/CodeAF/releases{/id}","deployments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Agent-Field/CodeAF/deployments","created_at":"2026-08-05T16:00:07Z","updated_at":"2026-09-23T17:31:44Z","pushed_at":"2026-09-23T18:02:56Z","git_url":"git://github.com/Agent-Field/CodeAF.git","ssh_url":"git@github.com:Agent-Field/CodeAF.git","clone_url":"https://github.com/Agent-Field/CodeAF.git","svn_url":"https://github.com/Agent-Field/CodeAF","homepage":"http://agentfield.ai/","size":196153,"stargazers_count":116,"watchers_count":116,"language":"Go","has_issues":true,"has_projects":true,"has_downloads":false,"has_wiki":false,"has_pages":false,"has_discussions":false,"forks_count":14,"mirror_url":null,"archived":false,"disabled":false,"open_issues_count":141,"license":{"key":"apache-2.0","name":"Apache License 2.0","spdx_id":"Apache-2.0","url":"https://api.github.com/licenses/apache-2.0","node_id":"MDc6TGljZW5zZTI="},"allow_forking":true,"is_template":false,"web_commit_signoff_required":false,"has_pull_requests":true,"pull_request_creation_policy":"all","topics":["agent-fleet","agent-harness","agentfield","agentic-coding","ai","ai-coding","cli-agent","coding-agent","coding-agents","coding-assistant","coding-cli","coding-harness","developer-tools","harness","harness-engineering","llm","open-models","open-source-models","software-factory","terminal-agent"],"visibility":"public","forks":14,"open_issues":141,"watchers":116,"default_branch":"dev","permissions":{"admin":true,"maintain":true,"push":true,"triage":true,"pull":true}},"body":"## Problem\n\n\"Run without asking\" has three names and two of them are hidden:\n\n- **Flag.** `--yolo` opens the gate for a whole process and must be typed at launch.\n- **Status line.** It shows a `YOLO` badge.\n- **Settings.** The Safety row `ask before running` offers `prompt` / `allow` / `deny`. The word a person knows, **yolo**, is not a choice: they must know that `allow` is YOLO.\n- **Commands.** No command switches it on `dev`. A person who wants to stop being asked mid-conversation has to open `/settings`, find Safety, and cycle a row whose values don't use the word the badge uses.\n\n## Ask\n\n1. **`/yolo` command.** It toggles the current conversation between asking and YOLO, and says the resulting posture in one line. With an argument it sets a posture by name. It must be discoverable in `/` completion and `/help`.\n2. **`yolo` in permissions.** The Safety row offers `yolo` as a named choice, with one vocabulary everywhere: the row, the badge, `/status`, `/status --json`, the manual. Options:\n   - **a.** Rename `allow` → `yolo` on the row. Keep `allow` accepted on disk and in `--approvals`-style inputs as an alias, so saved profiles keep meaning the same thing.\n   - **b.** Keep `allow` and add `yolo` as a displayed alias that writes `allow`.\n   - Recommended: **a**. The badge already says YOLO, and a person should see one word for one state.\n3. **Same safety as `--yolo`.** Named tool exceptions, shell rules and the critical-command floor still apply. `/yolo` must not be a way past the floor.\n4. **Scope.** The command changes the current conversation, live, sticky, and restored on `/resume`. The Safety row stays the install default. Both say which one they changed.\n\n5. **YOLO from every permission question.** Today the consent card (`AnswerOptions(QuestionConsent)`, `internal/session/answers.go`) offers `1 allow once` · `2 always` (this tool, this session) · `3 deny`. A person who is tired of being asked has to leave the question to find the setting. Add a fourth answer on every permission question: **`4 turn on yolo`**.\n   - It answers this call with allow, and switches the conversation's posture to YOLO: the same state `/yolo` sets, sticky and restored on `/resume`.\n   - It is marked `Widening`, drawn apart from the others like `always`, and never the default cursor, so muscle memory on `1` cannot land on it.\n   - The card's result line says what changed, e.g. `allowed · yolo on for this conversation · /yolo to turn it off`.\n   - The critical floor is untouched. A floor command's card does **not** offer `turn on yolo`, since the floor asks whatever the posture is.\n   - It applies on every surface that draws the consent question (chat card, home, the remote/phone sheet, a task room), and on the wire through the same answer set, so a replica offers exactly the same four.\n   - Questions that borrow the consent lane for something that is not a tool call (e.g. the stuck-turn question, which already drops `always`) don't offer it either.\n\n## Related\n\n- **#1071 (draft).** A per-conversation approvals posture with `/approvals` (alias `/yolo`) and an `alt+y` wheel. If it lands, it covers item 1 and most of 4. This issue then tracks item 2 (the `yolo` word in the permissions row and `/status`) plus confirming `/yolo` shows in completion and help.\n- **#1063 (merged).** Changing the Safety row now reaches the running gate, and `/status` names the gate as `prompt` / `allow` / `deny`, which is the vocabulary item 2 would change.\n- **#1035.** Headless and `--yolo` runs still can't answer the approval floor. Out of scope here, but the floor behaviour in item 3 must stay consistent with whatever that issue decides.\n\n## Acceptance\n\n- `/yolo` in a live conversation flips the next tool call's gate, shows the posture, survives `/resume`, and still asks on a floor command.\n- `/settings` → Safety shows `yolo` as a choice. An existing profile with `allow` reads as `yolo` with no migration step.\n- Badge, `/status`, JSON and the manual use the same word.\n- Every permission card that is not a floor command offers `turn on yolo`. Picking it runs the call, flips the posture, and the next non-floor call runs without a card.\n- Tests for each, plus the manual law.\n","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Agent-Field/CodeAF/issues/1074/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"timeline_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Agent-Field/CodeAF/issues/1074/timeline","performed_via_github_app":null,"state_reason":null,"pinned_comment":null}},"event":"cross-referenced"},{"id":31500768300,"node_id":"LE_lADOTu5AHM8AAAABRLcP0s8AAAAHVZeULA","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Agent-Field/CodeAF/issues/events/31500768300","actor":{"login":"santoshkumarradha","id":29346072,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjI5MzQ2MDcy","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/29346072?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/santoshkumarradha","html_url":"https://github.com/santoshkumarradha","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/santoshkumarradha/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/santoshkumarradha/following{/other_user}","gists_